## Commands

```bash
cd site && pnpm dev          # Local dev server (http://localhost:3000)
cd site && pnpm build        # Production build (SSG)
cd site && pnpm lint         # Lint check
```

## Post Format

Posts use YAML frontmatter:
```yaml
---
title: "Post Title"
subtitle: "Brief description"
author: "Nick Krzemienski"
date: "YYYY-MM-DD"
series_number: N
series_total: 32
github_repo: "https://github.com/krzemienski/repo-name"
tags:
  - AgenticDevelopment
  - ClaudeCode
---
```

Content uses standard Markdown with:
- Mermaid diagrams in fenced code blocks (render client-side with dark theme)
- SVG chart references: `![Chart](../visuals/svg/chart-name.svg)`
- Hero image references: `![Hero](../visuals/html/hero-name.html)`
- Real code snippets from production sessions (zero fabrication)

## Design System

**Theme:** Midnight Observatory (see DESIGN.md for full spec)

| Token | Hex | Role |
|-------|-----|------|
| Void Navy | #0f172a | Primary background |
| Slate Abyss | #1e293b | Cards, elevated surfaces |
| Indigo Pulse | #6366f1 | Primary accent, CTAs |
| Cyan Signal | #22d3ee | Metrics, data highlights |
| Cloud Text | #f1f5f9 | Headings, primary text |
| Slate Prose | #cbd5e1 | Body text |
| Mist Caption | #94a3b8 | Subtle text, metadata |

## Stitch MCP Integration

Stitch project ID stored in `stitch.json`. Usage patterns:
- **Hero images:** `generate_screen_from_text` with DESIGN.md Section 6 block
- **Social cards:** Generate Twitter (1200x628) and LinkedIn (1200x627) variants
- **Design exploration:** `generate_variants` with existing screens
- **Always** persist project ID after `create_project`
- **Always** include the design system prompt block from DESIGN.md Section 6

## Content Rules

- All code/output traceable to real Claude Code sessions
- No fabricated examples, no mock data
- Evidence-based claims with specific metrics
- First person, conversational but technically precise
- 1,500-2,500 words per post

## Product Site Architecture (project rule — see memory `project_site_product_architecture.md`)

`withagents.dev` is a **tiered product ecosystem**, not a single blog site.

- **Brand site** (`withagents.dev`) = writing + series + product catalog. Every product has a catalog entry at `/products/<slug>` that links OUT to the product's own site.
- **Product sites** each satisfy the **Product Site Template (PST)** contract regardless of tier:
  Hero → What-it-does (3 sentences) → Quick-start usage (≥2 inline examples) → Visual explainer (architecture/flow diagram) → How-it-works → Feature matrix → Install → Docs → Changelog → Links (GitHub, post, back-to-brand)
- **Tier ladder** (apply cheapest-first):
  - **Tier 1 — apex route** (default): `withagents.dev/products/<slug>` upgraded to full PST; works for every product at v1
  - **Tier 2 — subdomain via middleware rewrite** (`<slug>.withagents.dev`): when docs > 15 pages, distinct brand, or nested doc tree — uses same Next.js app via `site/src/proxy.ts` host-based rewrite
  - **Tier 3 — separate Vercel project**: only when isolation is required (different auth, framework, or interactive sandbox)
- **Middleware file is `site/src/proxy.ts`** (renamed from `middleware.ts` in Next.js 16). Tombstones live in `GONE_PATHS`.
- **Canonical content graph:** every product has exactly one blog post (the "writing"), exactly one catalog entry (the pivot), exactly one product site. `products.ts` is the graph root.
- **Validation IRON:** every product site passes three gates before launch — `functional-validation` (cURL + assert), `visual-inspection` (token parity screenshot at 375 / 768 / 1440), `e2e-validate` (cross-domain navigation: post → catalog → site → GitHub). No mocks, no test files.
- **Intentionally tombstoned:** `/products/deepest-plan` — retired during the 2026-04-20 products refactor; returns HTTP 410 via `site/src/proxy.ts` `GONE_PATHS`. Do not recreate unless the product actually ships with a real repo + post + catalog entry.
- **Currently thin:** `vf.withagents.dev` (docs only, no hero/landing above markdown), `consensus.withagents.dev` (does not exist). Both require PST upgrade before v1 launch.

See `plans/260421-1806-product-site-architecture/` for the executable plan.

